Expected loss is the *average credit loss that we would expect* from an exposure over *a given period of time.* It is calculated as the product of the #voir("probability-of-default"), the #voir("loss-given-default"), and #voir("exposure-at-default"). 

Expected loss is a key component of #voir("credit-risk") management and is used to estimate the amount of *capital* that a *bank* needs to hold *to cover potential credit losses*.

Expected loss is typically *covered by provisions and reserves* set aside as *part of normal business operations*.




